{number: 49}
{title: O Happy Day That Fixed My Choice}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] O happy day that fixed my choice
On Thee, my Savior [D7] and my [G] God!
Well may this glowing heart rejoice,
And tell its raptures [D7] all a-[G] broad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] Happy day, happy day,
When Jesus washed my [D7] sins a-[G] way!
He [D7] taught me how to watch and pray,
And live re-[G] joicing ev'ry day;
[G] Happy day, happy day,
When Jesus washed my [D7] sins a-[G] way!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
'Tis [G] done-the great transaction's done;
I am my Lord's, and [D7] He is [G] mine;
He drew me, and I followed on,
Rejoiced to own the [D7] call di-[G] vine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Now [G] rest, my long-divided heart;
Fixed on this blissful [D7] center, [G] rest;
Here have I found a nobler part,
Here heav’nly pleasures [D7] fill my [G] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
High [G] heav’n that hears the solemn vows,
That vow renewed shall [D7] daily [G] hear;
Till in life’s latest hour I bow,
And bless in death, a [D7] bond so [G] dear.
{end_of_verse}
